    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T14:43:54Z",
    "body": "QA swarm round 2 (#2582), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release: the same blocking, now in 2D and 5-axis kinds.\n\n- **5-Axis Parallel** on a plain 40 x 40 x 100 block ([q05-4axis.step](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q05-4axis/q05-4axis.step)), Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, BN-0600, all defaults: `generate` took **1040 s** (re-run by hand on len, 8 cores, otherwise loaded) and returned `status: ok`. In the agent's run, `parallel5d` and `multi_axis_rough` generates plus three `get_job` calls each hit the 3-minute MCP timeout (> 15 min with the server answering nothing), so the session could not save.\n- **2D Contour** around a 160 x 70 plate: 133 s by hand, 3-6 min in the agent's run (#3443).\n- **3D Finish** parallel and waterline on a 250 x 180 router part (q07): > 3 min each, and the following `get_job` also timed out.\n\nRepro: `import_model` the STEP, `load_machine {\"builtin\": \"Tormach 770MX + microARC 4\"}`, `set_stock {\"axis\": \"x\", \"box\": {\"dx\": 44, \"dy\": 44, \"dz\": 110}}`, `add_tool {\"catalog\": \"BN-0600\"}`, `add_operation {\"kind\": \"parallel5d\", ...}`, `generate`.\n- **3D Finish** waterline + scallop + pencil on the q02 mould core (STL import, 28692 facets, 770MX): the three generates and three `get_job` calls timed out over 21+ min; the session lost its unsaved job. (q02's STEP and .sc were refused with \"face Some(10) stands 5.089e-1 mm off its surface\": that is #3034, fixed on main by PR #3128 after the v0.25.0 tag.)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
