    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T08:27:24Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/3035-mcp-generate-worker · PR #3860 · pinned by background_generate::a_read_and_a_save_answer_while_a_generate_runs, background_generate::a_cancelled_generate_gets_no_answer_and_lands_nothing, background_generate::a_generate_whose_operation_changed_meanwhile_is_discarded · merges when reviewed\n\nThe PR is partial work (Refs #3035). The stdio MCP server now runs a generate on a worker thread. Other calls answer while it runs. `notifications/cancelled` drops it. Two parts stay open on this issue:\n- the run time of Rough12, Rest6 and Waterline6 on the mould core;\n- a cancel point inside the generators. A cancelled worker runs to its end now, and the session drops its result.\n\nThe staging of a rest operation still simulates the operations ahead of it on the session thread. That part still blocks other calls.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
